const waterLabels={0:"No common observation support",1:"Not classified as open water",2:"Water detected in both windows",3:"Water detected in wet window only",4:"Water detected in dry window only"};
const coverLabels={0:"No land-cover value",10:"Tree cover",20:"Shrubland",30:"Grassland",40:"Cropland (2021)",50:"Built-up",60:"Bare / sparse vegetation",70:"Snow / ice",80:"Permanent water class (2021)",90:"Herbaceous wetland",95:"Mangroves",100:"Moss / lichen"};
const notePages={
brief:`<h3>What the professor asked us to develop</h3><p class="context">Selected excerpts from the correspondence supplied for this project. These are directions for the work, not claims of completion.</p>
<blockquote>“Please consider the <mark>location of the archaeological landscapes</mark> rather than this idea of the centre or single monumental complex.”</blockquote><p>The comparison box is retained for the existing satellite statistics. A wider, checked landscape/catchment extent is still pending.</p>
<blockquote>“build a <mark>geodatabase or geopackage for each of the locations</mark>”</blockquote><p>One portable Angkor pilot is in the upload package. The other three GIS packages are not yet supplied.</p>
<blockquote>“integrate some <mark>landform or DEM data</mark>”</blockquote><p>The existing Copernicus surface heights are included and the four-box terrain audit is available. Drainage modelling and justified DEM fusion are not completed.</p>
<blockquote>“Please read the paper I sent through by <mark>Van Liere</mark>” and “read through the paper by <mark>Damian Evans</mark>”</blockquote><p>Paper notes now connect the six supplied works to mapping decisions, with page references, disagreements and questions to test. Source gaps and the OCR-assisted French review are documented.</p>
<blockquote>“filter the <mark>archaic features from more contemporary features</mark>”</blockquote><p>The professor described this as too complex for now. No ancient/modern classifier or dated feature inventory is presented.</p>
<hr class="note-rule"><h3>Landscape features beyond a single temple</h3><p>A sourced register of dispersed temples and hydraulic features is the next step. Names such as <em>wat</em> or <em>candi</em> alone cannot establish date or archaeological status.</p><p class="context">Selected directions from the project correspondence.</p>`,
readings:`<h3>Landform before labels</h3><p><mark>Van Liere 1980</mark> distinguishes floodplain use, bunded-field retention and receding-flood cultivation. Bunds can retain, spread or redirect water; their presence does not establish a formal irrigation network.</p><p class="context">Traditional Water Management in the Lower Mekong Basin, pp. 265–280; particularly pp. 271–273 and Figs. 2, 4–7.</p>
<h3>A specific lead for Sukhothai</h3><p><mark>Van Liere 1989</mark> distinguishes the hill-fed fan/terrace landscape from Yom River lowlands. Inspect these settings separately rather than treating Sukhothai as one flat plain. Field geometry cannot establish the identity or date of its makers.</p><p class="context">Mon-Khmer Approaches to the Environment, pp. 152–154; Figs. 9.6–9.7. The supplied scan lacks pp. 144–145 and duplicates pp. 146–147.</p>
<h3>Map the wider system, with evidence</h3><p><mark>Evans et al. 2007</mark> define a 2,848 km² watershed-based survey and combine image, map and survey sources. Feature inclusion required two different sources or ground/low-level aerial verification. Roads, canals and banks can have multiple roles.</p><p class="context">PNAS 104(36), pp. 14277–14282; evidence rule p. 14279, functions p. 14280. Our coarser imagery does not inherit their archaeological confidence.</p>
<h3>Water must leave fields as well as reach them</h3><p><mark>Groslier 1979</mark> reconstructs successive storage and redistribution systems using levels and connections. Earlier works can obstruct later flow. Water timing and drainage matter as well as total area.</p><p class="context">Text pp. 161–195; maps 1–7, pp. 196–202. French review used OCR with selected scan checks. His reconstructed lake margin is not a modern DEM threshold; p. 163 also flags historical levelling discrepancies.</p>
<h3>Compare field patches and productive spaces</h3><p><mark>Hawken &amp; Cobo Castillo</mark> distinguish the smaller patches around Pre Rup from the more coherent Phnom Bok matrix, alongside gardens and managed forests. These documented landscape units offer candidates for a focused seasonal comparison.</p><p class="context">Angkor’s Agrarian Economy, main text pp. 338–355; field cases pp. 344–350, Figs. 19.2–19.3. Modern FTW predictions are not dated archaeological patches.</p>
<h3>Trace interpretation and chronology</h3><p>The supplied <mark>Evans lidar manuscript</mark> explains how existing surveys can provide suitable reference evidence, and how superposition can support relative chronology. Record sources, scale, interpreter and uncertainty; choose follow-up that resolves a specific question.</p><p class="context">Main text to PDF p. 38; reference evidence pp. 17–21, chronology pp. 21–23, interpretation records p. 26. Publication details remain unverified. Our Copernicus surface model is not archaeological lidar.</p>
<hr class="note-rule"><h3>A question to test</h3><p>Within a documented field patch, do present seasonal water and vegetation patterns correspond to mapped sources, banks and outlets? Start with checked terrain and historical evidence. Seasonal connectivity is a method to evaluate; it has not yet been measured here.</p><p>These papers disagree on hydraulic function. Hawken &amp; Cobo Castillo, for example, challenge Van Liere’s assessment of thamnup irrigation capacity. The notes preserve these differences.</p><p><a href="documents/Reading_and_terrain_notes.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the nine-page paper notes and mapping plan ↗</a></p><p><a href="documents/Working_reading_notes.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Plain-text notes and references ↗</a></p>`,
progress:`<h3>What the shared package contains</h3><div class="status-row"><span class="status">Available</span><div>Earlier four-region exploratory satellite assessment, PowerPoint, map atlas, regional summaries and executed analysis notebook.</div></div><div class="status-row"><span class="status">Available</span><div>Angkor GeoPackage, nine rasters, QGIS project and source records. Native loading, CRS, relocation and render checks passed.</div></div><div class="status-row"><span class="status">Available</span><div>Terrain audit for the four original boxes.</div></div><div class="status-row"><span class="status">Available</span><div>Nine-page analytical notes on the six supplied works: arguments, disagreements, page references and mapping implications. The Van Liere 1989 scan gap, French OCR review and unverified manuscript publication details are documented.</div></div><div class="status-row"><span class="status pending">Pending</span><div>Equivalent portable GIS packages for Srei Santhor, Sukhothai and Prambanan.</div></div><div class="status-row"><span class="status pending">Pending</span><div>Wider checked landscape extents, native DEM quality review, terrain-source comparison and drainage analysis.</div></div><div class="status-row"><span class="status pending">Pending</span><div>Sourced temple/landscape-feature register and documented ancient/modern attribution.</div></div><div class="status-row"><span class="status pending">Unestimated</span><div>Accepted 2025 total agricultural, rice and irrigated areas. Independent thematic/elevation accuracy validation is incomplete.</div></div>
<h3>This explorer adds presentation, not new evidence</h3><p>Every map layer is a browser derivative of the existing Angkor upload package. No new scene, field survey, crop classifier or historical attribution is introduced.</p><p><a href="documents/source_manifest.json" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Compare source filenames and checksums ↗</a></p><p><button class="inline-files" data-open-files>Browse matching files →</button></p><p class="context">The shared research folder contains the GIS package, presentation, analysis notebook and reading notes.</p>`
};
let catalogue,map,baseImage,overlayImage,fieldLayer,activeBase="dry",activeOverlay="water",fieldGeneration=0;
const rasters = new Map(), fieldCache = new Map();
const fileLink=path=>catalogue?.driveUrl?catalogue.driveUrl:localPreview?`downloads/${path.split("/").map(encodeURIComponent).join("/")}`:null;
const detailsLink=(href,label)=>href?`<a href="${href}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">${label} ↗</a>`:`<span>${label}</span><small class="text-muted"> · shared Drive link pending</small>`;

function openSource(key){
  const s=sources[key];$("source-title").textContent=s.title;
  $("source-content").innerHTML=`<dl class="source-grid"><dt>Source</dt><dd>${s.provider}</dd><dt>Time represented</dt><dd>${s.date}</dd><dt>Resolution</dt><dd>${s.resolution}</dd><dt>How it was made</dt><dd>${s.method}</dd></dl><p class="source-warning">${s.limit}</p><p>${detailsLink(s.record,"Source record")} &nbsp;·&nbsp; ${detailsLink(s.url,"Dataset / method reference")}</p><p>${detailsLink(fileLink(s.file),"Original file in the research package")}</p><p class="text-muted">${catalogue.displayNote}</p><button id="all-sources-back">← All sources &amp; files</button>`;
  $("all-sources-back").onclick=openFiles;$("source-dialog").showModal();
}
function openFiles(){
  $("source-title").textContent="Sources & files";
  const papers=(catalogue.sharedFiles||[]).filter(file=>file.path.startsWith("04_")&&file.path.toLowerCase().endsWith(".pdf"));
  $("source-content").innerHTML=`<p>The explorer uses the same Angkor data as the current <strong>SHARE_WITH_SCOTT</strong> folder. Source filenames and raster SHA-256 checksums are retained. Web images and simplified outlines are display derivatives, not replacement GIS measurements.</p>
  <p>${detailsLink(fileLink(""),"Browse the shared research folder")}<br><small class="text-muted">Original GIS files, the presentation and analysis notebook are available in Google Drive. File links open the shared folder; use the listed filename to find each item.</small></p>
  <ul class="file-list"><li>${detailsLink("documents/Reading_and_terrain_notes.pdf","Reading and terrain notes")}<small>Nine-page paper summaries, page references, mapping implications and terrain audit.</small></li><li>${detailsLink(fileLink("01_Initial_assessment/Analysis_Notebook.html"),"Executed analysis: HTML")}<small>Saved code and outputs; complete rerun inputs are not all bundled.</small></li><li>${detailsLink(fileLink("01_Initial_assessment/Landscape_Assessment.pptx"),"Original PowerPoint")}<small>Earlier four-region exploratory assessment.</small></li><li>${detailsLink("documents/package_manifest.json","Current folder inventory")}<small>Current relative file paths and sizes; raster checksums are in the source manifest.</small></li></ul>
  ${papers.length?`<h3>Source papers supplied for the project</h3><ul class="file-list">${papers.map(file=>`<li>${detailsLink(fileLink(file.path),escapeText(file.path.split("/").pop()))}</li>`).join("")}</ul>`:""}
  <h3>Map layers</h3>${Object.entries(sources).map(([key,s])=>`<div class="source-card"><button data-source="${key}">${s.title}</button><p class="text-muted">${s.provider}</p></div>`).join("")}
  <p class="text-muted">Contains modified Copernicus Sentinel data (2025), ESA WorldCover 2021, JRC surface-water occurrence 1984–2024 and FTW predictions. Terrain produced using Copernicus WorldDEM-30 © DLR e.V. 2010–2014 and © Airbus Defence and Space GmbH 2014–2018, provided under COPERNICUS by the EU and ESA; all rights reserved.</p>`;
  document.querySelectorAll("[data-source]").forEach(button=>button.onclick=()=>openSource(button.dataset.source));$("source-dialog").showModal();
}
function renderLegend(){
  const row=(color,label)=>`<div class="legend-row"><span class="swatch" style="background:${color}"></span>${label}</div>`;
  const legends={water:row("#145d84","Water in both windows")+row("#3eabc2","Wet-window water only")+row("#c19149","Dry-window water only")+row("#aab1aa","No common observation support")+'<p class="legend-small">Common support: 84.1% · not a flood-event map</p>',vegetation:'<div class="ramp"></div><div class="ramp-labels"><span>Lower wet NDVI</span><span>Higher wet NDVI</span></div><p class="legend-small">Wet minus dry · ≥2 dates per window<br>54.1% coverage · not a crop classification</p>',landcover:row("#d3b66d","Cropland · 2021")+row("#2c5d41","Trees")+row("#a46359","Built-up")+row("#236ea1","Water")+'<p class="legend-small">Other ESA classes retained. Click to inspect.</p>',occurrence:'<div class="ramp" style="background:linear-gradient(90deg,#ebf2f4,#196797)"></div><div class="ramp-labels"><span>Rarely observed</span><span>100%</span></div><p class="legend-small">1984–2024 context · zero/nodata ambiguity</p>',support:row("#397667","≥2 accepted dates in each window")+row("#debb74","1 date in at least one window")+row("#757d78","No common support")+'<p class="legend-small">Coverage is not classification accuracy.</p>',none:'<p class="legend-small">No analytical overlay. Click to inspect the existing water and observation records.</p>'};
  $("legend").innerHTML=legends[activeOverlay];
}
function setBase(key){
  activeBase=key;if(baseImage)map.removeLayer(baseImage);baseImage=L.imageOverlay(`data/${key}.png`,catalogue.bounds,{pane:"base",interactive:false,attribution:"Copernicus / ESA"}).addTo(map);
  document.querySelectorAll("[data-base]").forEach(button=>{const active=button.dataset.base===key;button.classList.toggle("selected",active);button.setAttribute("aria-pressed",active);});
  const labels={dry:["Sentinel-2 · Feb–Apr 2025","Dry-window composite","Feb–Apr 2025"],wet:["Sentinel-2 · Aug–Oct 2025","Wet-window composite","Aug–Oct 2025"],terrain:["Copernicus GLO-30 · surface model","Broad surface heights","~30 m source · not bare-earth lidar"]};
  $("base-caption").textContent=labels[key][0];$("base-label").innerHTML=`${labels[key][1]} <span>${labels[key][2]}</span>`;
}
function setOverlay(key){activeOverlay=key;if(overlayImage)map.removeLayer(overlayImage);overlayImage=null;if(key!=="none")overlayImage=L.imageOverlay(`data/${key}.png`,catalogue.bounds,{pane:"analysis",opacity:Number($("opacity").value)/100,interactive:false}).addTo(map);renderLegend();}
async function raster(name){
  if(!rasters.has(name))rasters.set(name,(async()=>{const response=await fetch(`data/${name}.bin.gz`);if(!response.ok)throw Error("Inspection data unavailable");const bytes=pako.ungzip(new Uint8Array(await response.arrayBuffer()));return ["terrain","vegetation"].includes(name)?new Int16Array(bytes.buffer,bytes.byteOffset,bytes.byteLength/2):bytes;})());
  return rasters.get(name);
}
function pixel(latlng){const point=L.CRS.EPSG3857.project(latlng),b=catalogue.mercatorBounds;const x=Math.floor((point.x-b[0])/(b[2]-b[0])*catalogue.width),y=Math.floor((b[3]-point.y)/(b[3]-b[1])*catalogue.height);return x<0||y<0||x>=catalogue.width||y>=catalogue.height?null:y*catalogue.width+x;}
async function inspect(event){
  const i=pixel(event.latlng);if(i===null){L.popup().setLatLng(event.latlng).setContent('<p class="popup-title">Outside the comparison area</p><p class="popup-note">No analysis is supplied here. This box is not an archaeological landscape boundary.</p>').openOn(map);return;}
  const popup=L.popup().setLatLng(event.latlng).setContent("Reading source values…").openOn(map);
  try{const [water,dc,wc]=await Promise.all([raster("water"),raster("dry-count"),raster("wet-count")]);let extra="";
    if(activeOverlay==="vegetation"){const v=(await raster("vegetation"))[i];extra=`<div class="popup-row"><span>Wet minus dry NDVI</span><span>${v===-32768?"No ≥2-date support":(v/1000).toFixed(3)}</span></div>`;}
    if(activeOverlay==="landcover"){const v=(await raster("landcover"))[i];extra=`<div class="popup-row"><span>WorldCover 2021</span><span>${coverLabels[v]||"Unknown class"}</span></div>`;}
    if(activeOverlay==="occurrence"){const v=(await raster("occurrence"))[i];extra=`<div class="popup-row"><span>Long-term occurrence</span><span>${v===255?"Unknown":v===0?"0% / nodata ambiguity":v+"%"}</span></div>`;}
    if(activeBase==="terrain"){const v=(await raster("terrain"))[i];extra+=`<div class="popup-row"><span>Surface height, approx.</span><span>${v===-32768?"No value":(v/10).toFixed(1)+" m"}</span></div>`;}
    popup.setContent(`<p class="popup-title">${waterLabels[water[i]]||"Unknown"}</p><div class="popup-row"><span>Dry accepted dates</span><span>${dc[i]}</span></div><div class="popup-row"><span>Wet accepted dates</span><span>${wc[i]}</span></div>${extra}<p class="popup-note">A browser display sample, not a surveyed feature or archaeological date. Two windows do not prove year-round water.</p><a class="popup-link" href="#" id="popup-source">Source &amp; method →</a>`);
    setTimeout(()=>{const button=$("popup-source");if(button)button.onclick=e=>{e.preventDefault();openSource(activeOverlay==="none"?activeBase:activeOverlay);};},0);
  }catch(error){popup.setContent("Inspection could not load. The original GIS files remain available under Sources & files.");console.error(error);}
}
function overlap(a,b){return a[0]<=b.getEast()&&a[2]>=b.getWest()&&a[1]<=b.getNorth()&&a[3]>=b.getSouth();}
async function drawFields(){
  const generation=++fieldGeneration;fieldLayer.clearLayers();if(!$("fields").checked){$("fields-status").textContent="Zoom in to explore individual predictions.";return;}
  if(map.getZoom()<14){$("fields-status").textContent="Zoom to level 14 or closer to show field outlines.";return;}
  $("fields-status").textContent="Loading visible model predictions…";
  try{const bounds=map.getBounds();const tiles=catalogue.fieldTiles.filter(tile=>overlap(tile.bounds,bounds));
    const collections=await Promise.all(tiles.map(tile=>{if(!fieldCache.has(tile.file))fieldCache.set(tile.file,fetch("data/"+tile.file).then(async response=>{if(!response.ok)throw Error("Field tile unavailable");if(tile.file.endsWith(".gz"))return JSON.parse(pako.ungzip(new Uint8Array(await response.arrayBuffer()),{to:"string"}));return response.json();}));return fieldCache.get(tile.file);}));
    if(generation!==fieldGeneration||!$("fields").checked)return;const features=[];
    for(const collection of collections)for(const feature of collection.features){if(feature.bbox?overlap(feature.bbox,bounds):bounds.intersects(L.geoJSON(feature).getBounds()))features.push(feature);}
    if(features.length>12000){$("fields-status").textContent=`${features.length.toLocaleString()} predictions here. Zoom closer to draw outlines (limit 12,000).`;return;}
    fieldLayer.addData(features);$("fields-status").textContent=`${features.length.toLocaleString()} visible predictions · not verified boundaries.`;
  }catch(error){$("fields-status").textContent="Field data could not load. See source files.";console.error(error);}
}
function openNotes(open=true){$("notes").hidden=!open;$("notes-button").setAttribute("aria-expanded",String(open));$("workspace").classList.toggle("notes-open",open);}
function noteTab(name){$("notes-content").innerHTML=notePages[name];document.querySelectorAll("[data-note-tab]").forEach(button=>button.setAttribute("aria-selected",String(button.dataset.noteTab===name)));document.querySelectorAll("[data-open-files]").forEach(button=>button.onclick=openFiles);$("notes-content").scrollTop=0;}

async function start(){
  try{const response=await fetch("data/catalogue.json");if(!response.ok)throw Error("Map catalogue unavailable");catalogue=await response.json();
    map=L.map("map",{zoomControl:false,preferCanvas:true,minZoom:9,maxZoom:18,zoomSnap:.25,zoomDelta:.5,maxBounds:[[11,101],[16,107]],maxBoundsViscosity:.8});
    map.createPane("base").style.zIndex=200;map.createPane("analysis").style.zIndex=300;map.createPane("fields").style.zIndex=400;
    L.control.zoom({position:"topright"}).addTo(map);L.control.scale({position:"bottomright",imperial:false}).addTo(map);
    map.attributionControl.setPrefix(false);map.attributionControl.addAttribution('Sentinel-2 · Copernicus DEM · ESA WorldCover · JRC · FTW');
    L.rectangle(catalogue.bounds,{color:"#3c5244",weight:1,opacity:.5,fill:false,dashArray:"4 5",interactive:false}).addTo(map);
    fieldLayer=L.geoJSON(null,{pane:"fields",renderer:L.canvas({padding:.2,pane:"fields"}),style:{color:"#f6df92",weight:.8,opacity:.95,fillOpacity:0},onEachFeature:(feature,layer)=>{const p=feature.properties;layer.bindPopup(`<p class="popup-title">Modelled field ${escapeText(p.id)}</p><div class="popup-row"><span>Clipped polygon area</span><span>${p.area_ha.toFixed(3)} ha</span></div><div class="popup-row"><span>Source year</span><span>2025</span></div><div class="popup-row"><span>Coarse model score</span><span>${p.score===null?"Unknown":p.score+" / 100"}</span></div><p class="popup-note">Score is from a 500 m grid, not polygon accuracy. Not verified rice, irrigation, cadastral or ancient fields.</p>`);layer.on("click",event=>L.DomEvent.stopPropagation(event));}}).addTo(map);
    map.fitBounds(catalogue.bounds,{paddingTopLeft:[300,24],paddingBottomRight:[30,35]});setBase("dry");setOverlay("water");noteTab("brief");
    map.on("click",inspect);map.on("moveend",drawFields);map.on("mousemove",event=>$("coordinates").textContent=`${event.latlng.lat.toFixed(4)}° N  ${event.latlng.lng.toFixed(4)}° E`);
    document.querySelectorAll("[data-base]").forEach(button=>button.onclick=()=>setBase(button.dataset.base));$("overlay-select").onchange=event=>setOverlay(event.target.value);$("fields").onchange=drawFields;
    $("opacity").oninput=event=>{$("opacity-value").textContent=event.target.value+"%";if(overlayImage)overlayImage.setOpacity(event.target.value/100);};
    $("reset-view").onclick=()=>map.fitBounds(catalogue.bounds,{paddingTopLeft:innerWidth>760?[300,24]:[20,20],paddingBottomRight:[30,35]});
    $("layer-source").onclick=()=>openSource(activeOverlay==="none"?activeBase:activeOverlay);$("sources-button").onclick=openFiles;$("close-source").onclick=()=>$("source-dialog").close();$("source-dialog").onclick=event=>{if(event.target===$("source-dialog"))$("source-dialog").close();};
    $("notes-button").onclick=()=>openNotes($("notes").hidden);$("close-notes").onclick=()=>openNotes(false);document.querySelectorAll("[data-note-tab]").forEach(button=>button.onclick=()=>noteTab(button.dataset.noteTab));
    $("controls-toggle").onclick=()=>{const collapsed=!$("controls-body").hidden;$("controls-body").hidden=collapsed;$("controls-toggle").textContent=collapsed?"+":"−";$("controls-toggle").setAttribute("aria-expanded",String(!collapsed));document.querySelector(".map-controls").classList.toggle("collapsed",collapsed);};
    document.addEventListener("keydown",event=>{if(event.key==="Escape")openNotes(false);});
    if(innerWidth<=760){$("controls-body").hidden=true;$("controls-toggle").textContent="+";$("controls-toggle").setAttribute("aria-expanded","false");document.querySelector(".map-controls").classList.add("collapsed");map.fitBounds(catalogue.bounds,{padding:[20,20]});}
    $("loading").hidden=true;window.angkorExplorer={map,catalogue,sources,openNotes,openSource,noteTab,drawFields,check:()=>({layers:Object.keys(sources),fieldsTotal:catalogue.fieldCount,overlay:activeOverlay,base:activeBase,notesOpen:!$("notes").hidden})};
  }catch(error){$("loading").textContent="The map could not load. Please refresh or check your connection.";console.error(error);}
}
start();
